In Java, a socket is an endpoint for communication between two computers over a network. Java provides socket classes in the java.net package to implement client-server applications.

Main Classes
Socket – Used by the client to connect to a server.
ServerSocket – Used by the server to listen for incoming client connections.
How It Works
Server creates a ServerSocket on a port.
Server waits for a client using accept().
Client creates a Socket and connects to the server's IP and port.
Both sides exchange data using input and output streams.

Common Methods

| Class          | Method              | Purpose                       |
| -------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `ServerSocket` | `accept()`          | Waits for a client connection |
| `Socket`       | `getInputStream()`  | Receives data                 |
| `Socket`       | `getOutputStream()` | Sends data                    |
| `Socket`       | `close()`           | Closes the connection         |
